From f5c48434dc045467187c578a533c72686393d5e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 13:44:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 33/38] Carry the sibling fields the exporter already had the
 record open for

The S3 batch: 95 fields across 33 types the exporter already reaches (it
reads a sibling field of each on the same struct, in the same function),
just never read this particular one. Decode-and-carry only - no renderer
behaviour changed, no new parsing branch opened.

By area:

- Equation: baseline, versionInfo (EquationBlock).
- AutoNumber (page-number control only): pageNumberFormat/Superscript/
  UserSymbol/PrefixChar/SuffixChar (Span, set only in the existing
  AutoNumberType::Page arm of build_spans).
- Document/DocInfo: hwpmlVersion, isHwp3Variant, isHwpxVariant,
  extraStreamPaths, hwpxAuxEntryPaths (new top-level DocumentJson fields;
  the last two carry PATHS only, not the opaque roundtrip bytes - a reader
  can neither decode nor render them, and inlining would bloat the envelope
  for zero benefit).
- SectionDef: flags, columnSpacingHwpUnit, defaultTabSpacingHwpUnit,
  pageNumType, pictureNumStart, tableNumStart, equationNumStart, hideBorder,
  hideFill, hideEmptyLine (SectionDto).
- Footnote/Endnote (shared Span fields, set per-instance in
  build_note_blocks): noteBeforeChar, noteAfterChar, noteNumberShape.
- Header/Footer: listAttr, textWidthHwpUnit (HeaderFooterEntry, shared).
- MasterPage: isExtension, overlap, replaceBase, textWidthHwpUnit,
  textHeightHwpUnit (MasterPageDto).
- Picture/ImageAttr: borderX, borderY, brightness, contrast, effect,
  transparency, externalPath (ImageBlock).
- PageDef: marginHeader, marginFooter, marginGutter,
  paginationBottomTolerance, binding (PageGeometry - both the document-level
  one and each section's own).
- Paragraph/ParaShape/TabDef/Style/TextBox (ParaBlock): tabExtended,
  borderSpacing, tabDefAttr, autoTabLeft, autoTabRight, styleType, and the
  box* text-box fields (boxListAttr, boxVerticalAll, boxMargin{Left,Right,
  Top,Bottom}, boxMaxWidth) alongside the existing boxX/Y/W/H.
- CommonObjAttr (Placement, propagated to ImageBlock and ShapeBlock alike -
  read from the SAME outermost object every other Placement field comes
  from, never a group child's defaulted copy): objAttr, preventPageBreak,
  description.
- DrawingObjAttr: shadowAlpha (ShapeBlock).
- Numbering/NumberingHead/Bullet (ListInfo): numberingDefaultStart,
  numberingHeadAttr, numberingHeadTextDistance, bulletAttr,
  bulletTextDistance, bulletImageData.
- TabItem: fillType (TabStopDto).
- BorderFill: attr (BorderFillDto).
- Fill/SolidFill/GradientFill/ImageFill (ShapePath, gated the SAME way the
  existing `fill` hex is - an open path is not a filled figure, so none of
  these travel for one either): fillAlpha, patternColor, patternType, a
  nested `gradient` object, a nested `imageFill` object.
- ShapeBorderLine: outlineStyle (ShapeStrokeDto).
- Table: cellSpacingHwpUnit, rowSizes, outerMargin{Left,Right,Top,Bottom}
  (TableBlock).
- Cell: listHeaderWidthRef, textDirection, applyInnerMargin, fieldName
  (CellDto).

Nine fields from the manifest were NOT added, and are not silently dropped -
they don't fit the "decode and carry" shape:

- Table.dirty and local_resize_{rows,cols,cell_widths,cell_heights}: rhwp's
  own in-memory editing-session state. No parser file ever assigns them -
  only table_ops.rs/object_ops/table.rs/html_table_import.rs (editing and
  import commands) touch them, always initialising to false/empty. For the
  parse-then-export path this FFI actually runs, they are always
  false/empty - there is no document fact here to carry.
- Table.cell_grid: indexes into `table.cells` in ITS raw linear order, which
  this exporter never emits (rows/cols use row-major anchor cells with
  col_span/row_span instead). Exporting the raw indices would be an
  orphaned reference with nothing to resolve them against, and the
  occupancy they'd describe is already reconstructable from each cell's
  row/col + spans.
- Field.properties, extra_properties, ctrl_data_name: Control::Field is
  reached in this file only inside build_spans' hyperlink filter (`if
  f.field_type == FieldType::Hyperlink`), where ctrl_data_name in
  particular is almost always None - it is meaningful mainly for
  ClickHere/form fields, which nothing here currently loops over. A useful
  export needs a new loop over all Field controls regardless of type - a
  new branch, not a field add.

Placement lost its Copy/Clone derive (it now carries a String) - the two
call sites that used it more than once now take `&Placement`; behaviour is
unchanged.

New test: export_s3_b_tier_fields_reach_the_corpus scans every .hwp/.hwpx
under samples/ (340 files) and counts how many times each of 77 distinct
new JSON key strings appears (several of the 95 fields share a key name by
design, e.g. Header/Footer/MasterPage all emit textWidthHwpUnit). 60 of 77
were observed with real values; the 17 that were not are individually
explained in the test's own run output as corpus rarities rather than
wiring gaps (sibling fields from the SAME construction site - e.g.
patternColor/patternType/gradient alongside fillAlpha/imageFill, both from
collect_shape_paths's fill-detail block - DID fire, which is why an absent
sibling reads as "this document never set it" rather than "this code path
never runs"). Gate: fewer than half of the 77 keys missing across the
corpus, which would indicate a wiring bug rather than corpus rarity.

cargo check --lib and --tests: 0 errors, 0 warnings.
